IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `il-interpretation-time`
IMPORT domain
IMPORT `g4-council-membership`

-- g4-tests-membership.l4: tests for g4-council-membership.l4 (ss.20 to 23).  Expected values were decided from the Hebrew of
-- ss.20 to 23 (inputs/law.wiki lines 166-195) before the module was run: see work/g4/expectations.md.  Dates were computed with
-- Python's calendar, not with L4.  Each #ASSERT is one scenario; each #TRACE carries its expected outcome in the `-- EXPECT` comment above it.

§ `Tests for sections 20 to 23`

§§ `Names for the cases`

-- The eleven seats, by item number.
seat1 MEANS `seat 1: representative of the senior occupations-regulation division of the Ministry, the chair`
seat2 MEANS `seat 2: the Registrar`
seat3 MEANS `seat 3: the Commissioner for Standards, or an employee on the Commissioner's behalf`
seat4 MEANS `seat 4: employee of the Ministry of Energy and Infrastructure`
seat5 MEANS `seat 5: employee of the Ministry of Environmental Protection`
seat6 MEANS `seat 6: employee of the National Fire and Rescue Authority`
seat7 MEANS `seat 7: representative of the workers' organisation with the most licence holders`
seat8 MEANS `seat 8: representative of an employers' organisation`
seat9 MEANS `seat 9: representative of the organisation with the most engineers`
seat10 MEANS `seat 10: representative of the representative organisation under the Engineers and Technicians Law`
seat11 MEANS `seat 11: public representative`

-- Candidates.  Fields: holds the position | the competent Minister or Commissioner proposed | the Minister's opinion | a practical engineer or an engineer.
`a candidate who holds the position only`                  MEANS `Candidate for a seat on the Council` OF TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`a candidate who holds the position and was proposed`      MEANS `Candidate for a seat on the Council` OF TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE
`a candidate who was proposed but holds no position`       MEANS `Candidate for a seat on the Council` OF FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE
`a candidate who holds the position and the Minister so opines` MEANS `Candidate for a seat on the Council` OF TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE
`a candidate for whom the Minister so opines but who holds no position` MEANS `Candidate for a seat on the Council` OF FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE
`a candidate who holds the position and is an engineer`    MEANS `Candidate for a seat on the Council` OF TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE
`a candidate who holds nothing`                            MEANS `Candidate for a seat on the Council` OF FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE

-- Proceedings.  Fields: the offence makes the person unfit | the outcome.
`a conviction for an offence that makes the person unfit`            MEANS `Proceeding against a Council candidate or member for an offence` OF TRUE, `proceeding ended in a conviction`
`a conviction for an offence that does not make the person unfit`    MEANS `Proceeding against a Council candidate or member for an offence` OF FALSE, `proceeding ended in a conviction`
`a pending charge for an offence that makes the person unfit`        MEANS `Proceeding against a Council candidate or member for an offence` OF TRUE, `proceeding with no final judgment yet`
`a pending charge for an offence that does not make the person unfit` MEANS `Proceeding against a Council candidate or member for an offence` OF FALSE, `proceeding with no final judgment yet`
`a charge for an offence that makes the person unfit, ended in an acquittal` MEANS `Proceeding against a Council candidate or member for an offence` OF TRUE, `proceeding ended in a final judgment other than a conviction`
`a charge for an offence that does not make the person unfit, ended in an acquittal` MEANS `Proceeding against a Council candidate or member for an offence` OF FALSE, `proceeding ended in a final judgment other than a conviction`

§§ `Section 20: the eleven seats`

-- "מועצה בת 11 חברים": a council of 11 members; the eleven items are eleven different seats (T43: counted, no discrepancy).
#ASSERT `s 20 — the number of seats on the Council` EQUALS 11
#ASSERT count (nub `the eleven seats of the Council`) EQUALS 11

-- The chair is item (1), not the Registrar of item (2).
#ASSERT `s 20(1) — the seat is the chair's` seat1
#ASSERT NOT `s 20(1) — the seat is the chair's` seat2
#ASSERT NOT `s 20(1) — the seat is the chair's` seat11

-- Items 1, 2, 3 and 10 need only the position the item names.
#ASSERT `s 20 — the candidate satisfies the conditions of the seat` seat1 `a candidate who holds the position only`
#ASSERT NOT `s 20 — the candidate satisfies the conditions of the seat` seat1 `a candidate who holds nothing`
#ASSERT `s 20 — the candidate satisfies the conditions of the seat` seat2 `a candidate who holds the position only`
#ASSERT NOT `s 20 — the candidate satisfies the conditions of the seat` seat2 `a candidate who was proposed but holds no position`
#ASSERT `s 20 — the candidate satisfies the conditions of the seat` seat3 `a candidate who holds the position only`
#ASSERT NOT `s 20 — the candidate satisfies the conditions of the seat` seat3 `a candidate who holds nothing`
#ASSERT `s 20 — the candidate satisfies the conditions of the seat` seat10 `a candidate who holds the position only`
#ASSERT NOT `s 20 — the candidate satisfies the conditions of the seat` seat10 `a candidate who holds nothing`

-- Items 4, 5 and 6 need the position AND the proposal of the competent Minister or Commissioner.
#ASSERT `s 20 — the candidate satisfies the conditions of the seat` seat4 `a candidate who holds the position and was proposed`
#ASSERT NOT `s 20 — the candidate satisfies the conditions of the seat` seat4 `a candidate who holds the position only`
#ASSERT NOT `s 20 — the candidate satisfies the conditions of the seat` seat4 `a candidate who was proposed but holds no position`
#ASSERT `s 20 — the candidate satisfies the conditions of the seat` seat5 `a candidate who holds the position and was proposed`
#ASSERT NOT `s 20 — the candidate satisfies the conditions of the seat` seat5 `a candidate who holds the position only`
#ASSERT NOT `s 20 — the candidate satisfies the conditions of the seat` seat5 `a candidate who was proposed but holds no position`
#ASSERT `s 20 — the candidate satisfies the conditions of the seat` seat6 `a candidate who holds the position and was proposed`
#ASSERT NOT `s 20 — the candidate satisfies the conditions of the seat` seat6 `a candidate who holds the position only`
#ASSERT NOT `s 20 — the candidate satisfies the conditions of the seat` seat6 `a candidate who was proposed but holds no position`

-- Item 7: the position, and neither a practical engineer nor an engineer.
#ASSERT `s 20 — the candidate satisfies the conditions of the seat` seat7 `a candidate who holds the position only`
#ASSERT NOT `s 20 — the candidate satisfies the conditions of the seat` seat7 `a candidate who holds the position and is an engineer`
#ASSERT NOT `s 20 — the candidate satisfies the conditions of the seat` seat7 `a candidate who holds nothing`

-- Items 8, 9 and 11 rest on the Minister's opinion, an input; without it the seat is not satisfied, and the opinion alone is not enough.
#ASSERT `s 20 — the candidate satisfies the conditions of the seat` seat8 `a candidate who holds the position and the Minister so opines`
#ASSERT NOT `s 20 — the candidate satisfies the conditions of the seat` seat8 `a candidate who holds the position only`
#ASSERT NOT `s 20 — the candidate satisfies the conditions of the seat` seat8 `a candidate for whom the Minister so opines but who holds no position`
#ASSERT `s 20 — the candidate satisfies the conditions of the seat` seat9 `a candidate who holds the position and the Minister so opines`
#ASSERT NOT `s 20 — the candidate satisfies the conditions of the seat` seat9 `a candidate who holds the position only`
#ASSERT NOT `s 20 — the candidate satisfies the conditions of the seat` seat9 `a candidate for whom the Minister so opines but who holds no position`
#ASSERT `s 20 — the candidate satisfies the conditions of the seat` seat11 `a candidate who holds the position and the Minister so opines`
#ASSERT NOT `s 20 — the candidate satisfies the conditions of the seat` seat11 `a candidate who holds the position only`
#ASSERT NOT `s 20 — the candidate satisfies the conditions of the seat` seat11 `a candidate for whom the Minister so opines but who holds no position`

-- A candidate for one seat is judged by that seat's item: the engineer-excluding item 7 does not apply to item 8.
#ASSERT NOT `s 20 — the candidate satisfies the conditions of the seat` seat8 `a candidate who holds the position and is an engineer`
#ASSERT `s 20(7) — the candidate represents the workers' organisation with the most holders of grade 1, 2 or 3 licences and is neither a practical engineer nor an engineer` `a candidate who holds the position only`

§§ `Section 21: the bar on appointment`

#ASSERT `s 21 — the person is barred from appointment to the Council` (LIST `a conviction for an offence that makes the person unfit`)
#ASSERT NOT `s 21 — the person is barred from appointment to the Council` (LIST `a conviction for an offence that does not make the person unfit`)
#ASSERT `s 21 — the person is barred from appointment to the Council` (LIST `a pending charge for an offence that makes the person unfit`)
#ASSERT NOT `s 21 — the person is barred from appointment to the Council` (LIST `a pending charge for an offence that does not make the person unfit`)
-- "וטרם ניתן פסק דין סופי": once a final judgment has been given, an indictment no longer bars (T29, the s.21 side).
#ASSERT NOT `s 21 — the person is barred from appointment to the Council` (LIST `a charge for an offence that makes the person unfit, ended in an acquittal`)
#ASSERT NOT `s 21 — the person is barred from appointment to the Council` EMPTY
#ASSERT `s 21 — the person is barred from appointment to the Council` (LIST `a conviction for an offence that does not make the person unfit`, `a pending charge for an offence that makes the person unfit`)
#ASSERT NOT `s 21 — the person is barred from appointment to the Council` (LIST `a pending charge for an offence that does not make the person unfit`, `a charge for an offence that makes the person unfit, ended in an acquittal`)

-- The person who may be appointed: the seat's conditions, no s.21 bar, no s.29(b) bar.
#ASSERT `s 20, s 21, s 29(b) — the candidate may be appointed to the seat` seat4 `a candidate who holds the position and was proposed` EMPTY FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `s 20, s 21, s 29(b) — the candidate may be appointed to the seat` seat4 `a candidate who holds the position and was proposed` EMPTY TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 20, s 21, s 29(b) — the candidate may be appointed to the seat` seat4 `a candidate who holds the position only` EMPTY FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `s 20, s 21, s 29(b) — the candidate may be appointed to the seat` seat4 `a candidate who holds the position and was proposed` (LIST `a conviction for an offence that makes the person unfit`) FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `s 20, s 21, s 29(b) — the candidate may be appointed to the seat` seat4 `a candidate who holds the position and was proposed` (LIST `a pending charge for an offence that makes the person unfit`) FALSE
#ASSERT `s 20, s 21, s 29(b) — the candidate may be appointed to the seat` seat4 `a candidate who holds the position and was proposed` (LIST `a charge for an offence that makes the person unfit, ended in an acquittal`) FALSE

-- The duty to fill every seat (a council of eleven): eleven appointments of persons who may be appointed discharge it; ten leave the eleventh standing.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 20 — the Minister must appoint a member to each of the seats` `the eleven seats of the Council` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Minister` DOES `appoint a member of the Council` `the Minister` seat1 `a candidate who holds the position only` EMPTY FALSE FALSE AT 1
    PARTY `the Minister` DOES `appoint a member of the Council` `the Minister` seat2 `a candidate who holds the position only` EMPTY FALSE FALSE AT 2
    PARTY `the Minister` DOES `appoint a member of the Council` `the Minister` seat3 `a candidate who holds the position only` EMPTY FALSE FALSE AT 3
    PARTY `the Minister` DOES `appoint a member of the Council` `the Minister` seat4 `a candidate who holds the position and was proposed` EMPTY FALSE FALSE AT 4
    PARTY `the Minister` DOES `appoint a member of the Council` `the Minister` seat5 `a candidate who holds the position and was proposed` EMPTY FALSE FALSE AT 5
    PARTY `the Minister` DOES `appoint a member of the Council` `the Minister` seat6 `a candidate who holds the position and was proposed` EMPTY FALSE FALSE AT 6
    PARTY `the Minister` DOES `appoint a member of the Council` `the Minister` seat7 `a candidate who holds the position only` EMPTY FALSE FALSE AT 7
    PARTY `the Minister` DOES `appoint a member of the Council` `the Minister` seat8 `a candidate who holds the position and the Minister so opines` EMPTY FALSE FALSE AT 8
    PARTY `the Minister` DOES `appoint a member of the Council` `the Minister` seat9 `a candidate who holds the position and the Minister so opines` EMPTY FALSE FALSE AT 9
    PARTY `the Minister` DOES `appoint a member of the Council` `the Minister` seat10 `a candidate who holds the position only` EMPTY FALSE FALSE AT 10
    PARTY `the Minister` DOES `appoint a member of the Council` `the Minister` seat11 `a candidate who holds the position and the Minister so opines` EMPTY FALSE FALSE AT 11

-- Ten seats filled, the public representative's seat not: the duty stands.
-- EXPECT STANDING appoint a member of the Council
#TRACE `s 20 — the Minister must appoint a member to each of the seats` `the eleven seats of the Council` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Minister` DOES `appoint a member of the Council` `the Minister` seat1 `a candidate who holds the position only` EMPTY FALSE FALSE AT 1
    PARTY `the Minister` DOES `appoint a member of the Council` `the Minister` seat2 `a candidate who holds the position only` EMPTY FALSE FALSE AT 2
    PARTY `the Minister` DOES `appoint a member of the Council` `the Minister` seat3 `a candidate who holds the position only` EMPTY FALSE FALSE AT 3
    PARTY `the Minister` DOES `appoint a member of the Council` `the Minister` seat4 `a candidate who holds the position and was proposed` EMPTY FALSE FALSE AT 4
    PARTY `the Minister` DOES `appoint a member of the Council` `the Minister` seat5 `a candidate who holds the position and was proposed` EMPTY FALSE FALSE AT 5
    PARTY `the Minister` DOES `appoint a member of the Council` `the Minister` seat6 `a candidate who holds the position and was proposed` EMPTY FALSE FALSE AT 6
    PARTY `the Minister` DOES `appoint a member of the Council` `the Minister` seat7 `a candidate who holds the position only` EMPTY FALSE FALSE AT 7
    PARTY `the Minister` DOES `appoint a member of the Council` `the Minister` seat8 `a candidate who holds the position and the Minister so opines` EMPTY FALSE FALSE AT 8
    PARTY `the Minister` DOES `appoint a member of the Council` `the Minister` seat9 `a candidate who holds the position and the Minister so opines` EMPTY FALSE FALSE AT 9
    PARTY `the Minister` DOES `appoint a member of the Council` `the Minister` seat10 `a candidate who holds the position only` EMPTY FALSE FALSE AT 10

-- An item-4 seat filled by an employee who was not proposed does not discharge the duty for that seat.
-- EXPECT STANDING appoint a member of the Council
#TRACE `s 20 — the Minister must appoint a member to the seat` seat4 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Minister` DOES `appoint a member of the Council` `the Minister` seat4 `a candidate who holds the position only` EMPTY FALSE FALSE AT 4

-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 20 — the Minister must appoint a member to the seat` seat4 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Minister` DOES `appoint a member of the Council` `the Minister` seat4 `a candidate who holds the position and was proposed` EMPTY FALSE FALSE AT 4

-- A candidate barred by section 29(b) (the flag after the proceedings list) is not a person who may be appointed: no discharge.
-- EXPECT STANDING appoint a member of the Council
#TRACE `s 20 — the Minister must appoint a member to the seat` seat4 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Minister` DOES `appoint a member of the Council` `the Minister` seat4 `a candidate who holds the position and was proposed` EMPTY TRUE FALSE AT 4

-- The prohibition of s.21: appointing a person barred by conviction or by a pending charge is a breach.
-- EXPECT BREACH s 21
#TRACE `s 21 — the Minister must not appoint to the Council a person barred by section 21` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Minister` DOES `appoint a member of the Council` `the Minister` seat4 `a candidate who holds the position and was proposed` (LIST `a conviction for an offence that makes the person unfit`) FALSE FALSE AT 4

-- EXPECT BREACH s 21
#TRACE `s 21 — the Minister must not appoint to the Council a person barred by section 21` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Minister` DOES `appoint a member of the Council` `the Minister` seat4 `a candidate who holds the position and was proposed` (LIST `a pending charge for an offence that makes the person unfit`) FALSE FALSE AT 4

-- Appointing a person who is not barred is no breach: the prohibition stays standing for the next appointment.
-- EXPECT STANDING appoint a member of the Council
#TRACE `s 21 — the Minister must not appoint to the Council a person barred by section 21` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Minister` DOES `appoint a member of the Council` `the Minister` seat4 `a candidate who holds the position and was proposed` EMPTY FALSE FALSE AT 4

-- An acquittal ends the bar: appointing that person is no breach.
-- EXPECT STANDING appoint a member of the Council
#TRACE `s 21 — the Minister must not appoint to the Council a person barred by section 21` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Minister` DOES `appoint a member of the Council` `the Minister` seat4 `a candidate who holds the position and was proposed` (LIST `a charge for an offence that makes the person unfit, ended in an acquittal`) FALSE FALSE AT 4

§§ `Section 22: the four-year term (P19, kind V, IL s.10(b) from the day of appointment, IL s.10(c) not applied)`

-- First term: four years after the day of appointment; the last day is inside the term.
#ASSERT `s 22 — the last day of the term of office when` 1 `terms of four years run from the day` (YMD 2025 7 16) EQUALS YMD 2029 7 16
#ASSERT `s 22 — the last day of the term of office when` 1 `terms of four years run from the day` (YMD 2024 2 29) EQUALS YMD 2028 2 29
#ASSERT `s 22 — the last day of the term of office when` 1 `terms of four years run from the day` (YMD 2020 2 29) EQUALS YMD 2024 2 29
-- 2100 is not a leap year: the month's last day (s.10(b)).
#ASSERT `s 22 — the last day of the term of office when` 1 `terms of four years run from the day` (YMD 2096 2 29) EQUALS YMD 2100 2 28
-- A Saturday end (2029-06-30) is not moved: kind V, IL s.10(c) not applied.
#ASSERT `s 22 — the last day of the term of office when` 1 `terms of four years run from the day` (YMD 2025 6 30) EQUALS YMD 2029 6 30
-- Each further term is four years on from the end of the one before (reading A).
#ASSERT `s 22 — the last day of the term of office when` 2 `terms of four years run from the day` (YMD 2025 7 16) EQUALS YMD 2033 7 16
#ASSERT `s 22 — the last day of the term of office when` 3 `terms of four years run from the day` (YMD 2025 7 16) EQUALS YMD 2037 7 16

-- By seat: the Registrar has no end by term ("למעט הרשם"); every other seat has one.
#ASSERT `s 22 — the seat has a term of four years` seat1
#ASSERT `s 22 — the seat has a term of four years` seat11
#ASSERT NOT `s 22 — the seat has a term of four years` seat2
#ASSERT `s 22 — the last day of the term of office of the member in the seat` seat4 `appointed on the day` (YMD 2025 7 16) `, after` 0 `further terms granted` EQUALS JUST (YMD 2029 7 16)
#ASSERT `s 22 — the last day of the term of office of the member in the seat` seat4 `appointed on the day` (YMD 2025 7 16) `, after` 1 `further terms granted` EQUALS JUST (YMD 2033 7 16)
#ASSERT `s 22 — the last day of the term of office of the member in the seat` seat2 `appointed on the day` (YMD 2025 7 16) `, after` 0 `further terms granted` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 22 — the last day of the term of office of the member in the seat` seat2 `appointed on the day` (YMD 2025 7 16) `, after` 2 `further terms granted` EQUALS NOTHING

-- FORK F-22-V, the alternative: IL s.10(c) applied.  Rest days 2029-06-30 (Saturday) and 2029-07-01 (Sunday): the end moves to Monday 2029-07-02.
`a calendar with the Saturday and the Sunday after the first term of an appointment on 2025-06-30` MEANS `Calendar of rest days` OF (LIST (YMD 2029 6 30), (YMD 2029 7 1))
`a calendar with only the Saturday` MEANS `Calendar of rest days` OF (LIST (YMD 2029 6 30))
`a calendar with no rest days` MEANS `Calendar of rest days` OF EMPTY
#ASSERT `s 22, alternative reading — the last day of the first term when IL s.10(c) moves an end that falls on a day of rest, appointed on` (YMD 2025 6 30) `with days of rest` `a calendar with the Saturday and the Sunday after the first term of an appointment on 2025-06-30` EQUALS YMD 2029 7 2
#ASSERT `s 22, alternative reading — the last day of the first term when IL s.10(c) moves an end that falls on a day of rest, appointed on` (YMD 2025 6 30) `with days of rest` `a calendar with only the Saturday` EQUALS YMD 2029 7 1
#ASSERT `s 22, alternative reading — the last day of the first term when IL s.10(c) moves an end that falls on a day of rest, appointed on` (YMD 2025 6 30) `with days of rest` `a calendar with no rest days` EQUALS YMD 2029 6 30
-- A Monday end is unaffected by the same calendar.
#ASSERT `s 22, alternative reading — the last day of the first term when IL s.10(c) moves an end that falls on a day of rest, appointed on` (YMD 2025 7 16) `with days of rest` `a calendar with the Saturday and the Sunday after the first term of an appointment on 2025-06-30` EQUALS YMD 2029 7 16

-- FORK F-22-length, the alternative: the Minister fixes the length of each further term.
#ASSERT `s 22, alternative reading — the last day of a term when the Minister fixes each further term, appointed on` (YMD 2025 7 16) `with further terms of` EMPTY EQUALS YMD 2029 7 16
#ASSERT `s 22, alternative reading — the last day of a term when the Minister fixes each further term, appointed on` (YMD 2025 7 16) `with further terms of` (LIST 2) EQUALS YMD 2031 7 16
#ASSERT `s 22, alternative reading — the last day of a term when the Minister fixes each further term, appointed on` (YMD 2025 7 16) `with further terms of` (LIST 1) EQUALS YMD 2030 7 16
#ASSERT `s 22, alternative reading — the last day of a term when the Minister fixes each further term, appointed on` (YMD 2025 7 16) `with further terms of` (LIST 2, 1) EQUALS YMD 2032 7 16

-- The Minister's power to extend: it exists for a seat with a term, not for the Registrar's seat.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 22 — the Minister may extend the term of the member in the seat` seat4 "member-4" AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Minister` DOES `extend the term of a member of the Council` `the Minister` "member-4" AT 5

-- EXPECT STANDING extend the term of a member of the Council
#TRACE `s 22 — the Minister may extend the term of the member in the seat` seat4 "member-4" AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 400)

-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 22 — the Minister may extend the term of the member in the seat` seat2 "the-registrar" AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 400)

§§ `Section 23(a): service that ends of its own accord`

-- Events.  Fields: resignation delivered | ceased to be employee or member | public representative appointed a State employee.
`events: a resignation on 2026-03-01`                 MEANS `Events ending a member's service under section 23(a)` OF (JUST (YMD 2026 3 1)), NOTHING, NOTHING
`events: ceased to be an employee on 2026-05-01`       MEANS `Events ending a member's service under section 23(a)` OF NOTHING, (JUST (YMD 2026 5 1)), NOTHING
`events: a resignation on 2026-03-01 and ceasing on 2026-05-01` MEANS `Events ending a member's service under section 23(a)` OF (JUST (YMD 2026 3 1)), (JUST (YMD 2026 5 1)), NOTHING
`events: a State employee appointment on 2026-02-10 and ceasing on 2026-01-05` MEANS `Events ending a member's service under section 23(a)` OF NOTHING, (JUST (YMD 2026 1 5)), (JUST (YMD 2026 2 10))
`events: a State employee appointment on 2026-02-10 only` MEANS `Events ending a member's service under section 23(a)` OF NOTHING, NOTHING, (JUST (YMD 2026 2 10))
`events: none` MEANS `Events ending a member's service under section 23(a)` OF NOTHING, NOTHING, NOTHING

#ASSERT `s 23(a)(1) — the day the member's service ended by resignation` `events: a resignation on 2026-03-01` EQUALS JUST (YMD 2026 3 1)
#ASSERT `s 23(a)(1) — the day the member's service ended by resignation` `events: none` EQUALS NOTHING
-- Seats 1 to 10: ceasing to be an employee of the ministry or a member of the body represented.
#ASSERT `s 23(a)(2) — the day the member's service ended by ceasing to be employee or member, or by becoming a State employee` seat4 `events: ceased to be an employee on 2026-05-01` EQUALS JUST (YMD 2026 5 1)
#ASSERT `s 23(a)(2) — the day the member's service ended by ceasing to be employee or member, or by becoming a State employee` seat7 `events: ceased to be an employee on 2026-05-01` EQUALS JUST (YMD 2026 5 1)
-- Becoming a State employee does nothing to a member of seats 1 to 10.
#ASSERT `s 23(a)(2) — the day the member's service ended by ceasing to be employee or member, or by becoming a State employee` seat4 `events: a State employee appointment on 2026-02-10 only` EQUALS NOTHING
-- Seat 11, the public representative: the State-employee appointment; ceasing to be a member of a body is not a ground.
#ASSERT `s 23(a)(2) — the day the member's service ended by ceasing to be employee or member, or by becoming a State employee` seat11 `events: a State employee appointment on 2026-02-10 only` EQUALS JUST (YMD 2026 2 10)
#ASSERT `s 23(a)(2) — the day the member's service ended by ceasing to be employee or member, or by becoming a State employee` seat11 `events: ceased to be an employee on 2026-05-01` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 23(a)(2) — the day the member's service ended by ceasing to be employee or member, or by becoming a State employee` seat11 `events: a State employee appointment on 2026-02-10 and ceasing on 2026-01-05` EQUALS JUST (YMD 2026 2 10)
-- The earlier of two: resignation 2026-03-01 before ceasing 2026-05-01.
#ASSERT `s 23(a) — the day the member ceased to serve under section 23(a)` seat4 `events: a resignation on 2026-03-01 and ceasing on 2026-05-01` EQUALS JUST (YMD 2026 3 1)
#ASSERT `s 23(a) — the day the member ceased to serve under section 23(a)` seat4 `events: ceased to be an employee on 2026-05-01` EQUALS JUST (YMD 2026 5 1)
#ASSERT `s 23(a) — the day the member ceased to serve under section 23(a)` seat4 `events: none` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 23(a) — the day the member ceased to serve under section 23(a)` seat11 `events: a State employee appointment on 2026-02-10 and ceasing on 2026-01-05` EQUALS JUST (YMD 2026 2 10)

§§ `Sections 22 and 23: whether a member is serving on a day`

-- Fields: reference | seat | appointed on | further terms | events | removed on.
`a seat 4 member appointed 2025-07-16, never extended, no event`   MEANS `Service record of a member of the Council` OF "m4", seat4, (YMD 2025 7 16), 0, `events: none`, NOTHING
`a seat 4 member appointed 2025-07-16, extended once`              MEANS `Service record of a member of the Council` OF "m4", seat4, (YMD 2025 7 16), 1, `events: none`, NOTHING
`a seat 4 member appointed 2025-07-16 who resigned on 2026-03-01`  MEANS `Service record of a member of the Council` OF "m4", seat4, (YMD 2025 7 16), 0, `events: a resignation on 2026-03-01`, NOTHING
`a seat 4 member appointed 2025-07-16 and removed on 2027-01-10`   MEANS `Service record of a member of the Council` OF "m4", seat4, (YMD 2025 7 16), 0, `events: none`, (JUST (YMD 2027 1 10))
`the Registrar appointed 2025-07-16`                               MEANS `Service record of a member of the Council` OF "reg", seat2, (YMD 2025 7 16), 0, `events: none`, NOTHING

#ASSERT NOT `s 22, s 23 — the member is serving on the day` (YMD 2025 7 15) `according to` `a seat 4 member appointed 2025-07-16, never extended, no event`
#ASSERT `s 22, s 23 — the member is serving on the day` (YMD 2025 7 16) `according to` `a seat 4 member appointed 2025-07-16, never extended, no event`
#ASSERT `s 22, s 23 — the member is serving on the day` (YMD 2029 7 16) `according to` `a seat 4 member appointed 2025-07-16, never extended, no event`
#ASSERT NOT `s 22, s 23 — the member is serving on the day` (YMD 2029 7 17) `according to` `a seat 4 member appointed 2025-07-16, never extended, no event`
#ASSERT `s 22, s 23 — the member is serving on the day` (YMD 2033 7 16) `according to` `a seat 4 member appointed 2025-07-16, extended once`
#ASSERT NOT `s 22, s 23 — the member is serving on the day` (YMD 2033 7 17) `according to` `a seat 4 member appointed 2025-07-16, extended once`
-- Resignation delivered on 2026-03-01: not serving from that day (reading taken, F-day); the alternative counts the day.
#ASSERT `s 22, s 23 — the member is serving on the day` (YMD 2026 2 28) `according to` `a seat 4 member appointed 2025-07-16 who resigned on 2026-03-01`
#ASSERT NOT `s 22, s 23 — the member is serving on the day` (YMD 2026 3 1) `according to` `a seat 4 member appointed 2025-07-16 who resigned on 2026-03-01`
#ASSERT `s 22, s 23, alternative reading — the member is serving on the day` (YMD 2026 3 1) `counting the day service ends as a day of service, according to` `a seat 4 member appointed 2025-07-16 who resigned on 2026-03-01`
#ASSERT NOT `s 22, s 23, alternative reading — the member is serving on the day` (YMD 2026 3 2) `counting the day service ends as a day of service, according to` `a seat 4 member appointed 2025-07-16 who resigned on 2026-03-01`
-- Removal on 2027-01-10.
#ASSERT `s 22, s 23 — the member is serving on the day` (YMD 2027 1 9) `according to` `a seat 4 member appointed 2025-07-16 and removed on 2027-01-10`
#ASSERT NOT `s 22, s 23 — the member is serving on the day` (YMD 2027 1 10) `according to` `a seat 4 member appointed 2025-07-16 and removed on 2027-01-10`
#ASSERT `s 22, s 23, alternative reading — the member is serving on the day` (YMD 2027 1 10) `counting the day service ends as a day of service, according to` `a seat 4 member appointed 2025-07-16 and removed on 2027-01-10`
-- The Registrar's seat has no end by term.
#ASSERT `s 22, s 23 — the member is serving on the day` (YMD 2040 1 1) `according to` `the Registrar appointed 2025-07-16`
#ASSERT NOT `s 22, s 23 — the member is serving on the day` (YMD 2025 7 15) `according to` `the Registrar appointed 2025-07-16`

-- FORK F-20-2: the Registrar's membership and the office.  Reading A: no end with the office; he serves until the Minister removes him (s.23(b)(3)).
-- The Registrar ceased to be the Registrar on 2026-03-01 and has not been removed: serving on 2026-03-15 under reading A, not under the alternative.
#ASSERT `s 22, s 23 — the member is serving on the day` (YMD 2026 3 15) `according to` `the Registrar appointed 2025-07-16`
#ASSERT NOT `s 20(2), s 22, alternative reading — the Registrar's membership continues on the day` (YMD 2026 3 15) `, the office having ended on` (JUST (YMD 2026 3 1))
#ASSERT `s 20(2), s 22, alternative reading — the Registrar's membership continues on the day` (YMD 2026 2 28) `, the office having ended on` (JUST (YMD 2026 3 1))
#ASSERT `s 20(2), s 22, alternative reading — the Registrar's membership continues on the day` (YMD 2040 1 1) `, the office having ended on` NOTHING

§§ `Section 23(b): the Minister must remove the member`

-- Fields: proceedings | permanently unable | still satisfies the conditions of the seat | barred by section 29(b) | has not already ceased under section 23(a).
`a member with no ground`                       MEANS `Facts about a member for section 23(b)` OF EMPTY, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE
`a member convicted of an offence that makes the member unfit` MEANS `Facts about a member for section 23(b)` OF (LIST `a conviction for an offence that makes the person unfit`), FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE
`a member under a pending charge that makes the member unfit` MEANS `Facts about a member for section 23(b)` OF (LIST `a pending charge for an offence that makes the person unfit`), FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE
`a member charged and later acquitted`          MEANS `Facts about a member for section 23(b)` OF (LIST `a charge for an offence that makes the person unfit, ended in an acquittal`), FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE
`a member convicted of an offence that does not make the member unfit` MEANS `Facts about a member for section 23(b)` OF (LIST `a conviction for an offence that does not make the person unfit`), FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE
`a member charged with an offence that does not make the member unfit, later acquitted` MEANS `Facts about a member for section 23(b)` OF (LIST `a charge for an offence that does not make the person unfit, ended in an acquittal`), FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE
`a member permanently unable`                   MEANS `Facts about a member for section 23(b)` OF EMPTY, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE
`a member who no longer satisfies the conditions of the seat` MEANS `Facts about a member for section 23(b)` OF EMPTY, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE
`a member barred by section 29(b)`              MEANS `Facts about a member for section 23(b)` OF EMPTY, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE

#ASSERT NOT `s 23(b) — a ground for removal exists` `a member with no ground`
#ASSERT `s 23(b) — a ground for removal exists` `a member convicted of an offence that makes the member unfit`
#ASSERT `s 23(b) — a ground for removal exists` `a member under a pending charge that makes the member unfit`
#ASSERT NOT `s 23(b) — a ground for removal exists` `a member convicted of an offence that does not make the member unfit`
#ASSERT NOT `s 23(b) — a ground for removal exists` `a member charged with an offence that does not make the member unfit, later acquitted`
#ASSERT `s 23(b) — a ground for removal exists` `a member permanently unable`
#ASSERT `s 23(b) — a ground for removal exists` `a member who no longer satisfies the conditions of the seat`
#ASSERT `s 23(b) — a ground for removal exists` `a member barred by section 29(b)`

-- T29, the discriminating case: charged and later acquitted.  s.21 would allow the appointment; the words of s.23(b)(1) still require removal (reading A).
#ASSERT NOT `s 21 — the person is barred from appointment to the Council` (LIST `a charge for an offence that makes the person unfit, ended in an acquittal`)
#ASSERT `s 23(b) — a ground for removal exists` `a member charged and later acquitted`
#ASSERT `s 23(b)(3) — the member ceased to meet a condition required for the appointment` `a member barred by section 29(b)`
-- The alternative mirroring s.21: no ground after the acquittal.
#ASSERT NOT `s 23(b), alternative reading — a ground for removal exists` `a member charged and later acquitted`
#ASSERT `s 23(b), alternative reading — a ground for removal exists` `a member under a pending charge that makes the member unfit`
#ASSERT `s 23(b), alternative reading — a ground for removal exists` `a member convicted of an offence that makes the member unfit`
-- (b)(3), the conditions of appointment: reading B counts the s.29(b) bar, the alternative only the conditions of the seat.
#ASSERT NOT `s 23(b)(3), alternative reading — the member ceased to satisfy the conditions of the seat` `a member barred by section 29(b)`
#ASSERT `s 23(b)(3), alternative reading — the member ceased to satisfy the conditions of the seat` `a member who no longer satisfies the conditions of the seat`

-- CONTRADICTION C-23a-b3: a member who has already ceased to serve under (a): the ground exists, but (reading A) there is nothing to remove him from.
`a member who ceased to be an employee of his ministry and so no longer satisfies the seat` MEANS `Facts about a member for section 23(b)` OF EMPTY, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
#ASSERT `s 23(b) — a ground for removal exists` `a member who ceased to be an employee of his ministry and so no longer satisfies the seat`
#ASSERT NOT `s 23(b) — the Minister's duty to remove the member arises` `a member who ceased to be an employee of his ministry and so no longer satisfies the seat`
#ASSERT `s 23(b), alternative reading — the Minister's duty to remove the member arises whether or not the member has ceased under section 23(a)` `a member who ceased to be an employee of his ministry and so no longer satisfies the seat`
#ASSERT `s 23(b) — the Minister's duty to remove the member arises` `a member permanently unable`
#ASSERT NOT `s 23(b) — the Minister's duty to remove the member arises` `a member with no ground`

-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 23(b) — the Minister must remove the member by written notice` "m4" `a member who ceased to be an employee of his ministry and so no longer satisfies the seat` AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 400)

-- The duty, traced.  A removal by written notice after the opportunity to respond, close to the time: fulfilled.
-- Fields of the act: the member | by written notice | after the opportunity | close to the time.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 23(b) — the Minister must remove the member by written notice` "m4" `a member permanently unable` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Minister` DOES `remove a member of the Council from office` `the Minister` "m4" TRUE TRUE TRUE AT 20

-- A late removal still removes the member and discharges the duty, but is a breach of "close to the time" (kind N: a judgement on the act).
-- EXPECT BREACH s 23(b): the member was not removed close to the time
#TRACE `s 23(b) — the Minister must remove the member by written notice` "m4" `a member permanently unable` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Minister` DOES `remove a member of the Council from office` `the Minister` "m4" TRUE TRUE FALSE AT 900

-- A removal that was not in writing, or not after the opportunity to respond, is not the removal the section requires: the duty stands.
-- EXPECT STANDING remove a member of the Council from office
#TRACE `s 23(b) — the Minister must remove the member by written notice` "m4" `a member permanently unable` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Minister` DOES `remove a member of the Council from office` `the Minister` "m4" FALSE TRUE TRUE AT 20

-- EXPECT STANDING remove a member of the Council from office
#TRACE `s 23(b) — the Minister must remove the member by written notice` "m4" `a member permanently unable` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Minister` DOES `remove a member of the Council from office` `the Minister` "m4" TRUE FALSE TRUE AT 20

-- Removal of a different member does not discharge it.
-- EXPECT STANDING remove a member of the Council from office
#TRACE `s 23(b) — the Minister must remove the member by written notice` "m4" `a member permanently unable` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Minister` DOES `remove a member of the Council from office` `the Minister` "m9" TRUE TRUE TRUE AT 20

-- No ground, no duty.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 23(b) — the Minister must remove the member by written notice` "m4" `a member with no ground` AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 400)

-- No time is stated ("בסמוך" is vague), so waiting breaches nothing by itself: the duty stands.
-- EXPECT STANDING remove a member of the Council from office
#TRACE `s 23(b) — the Minister must remove the member by written notice` "m4" `a member permanently unable` AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 4000)

-- T29 traced: the acquitted member's removal is owed under reading A.
-- EXPECT STANDING remove a member of the Council from office
#TRACE `s 23(b) — the Minister must remove the member by written notice` "m4" `a member charged and later acquitted` AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 400)

§§ `Section 23(c): removal for absence`

-- Meeting helpers.  Fields: the day | held by a subcommittee | the member was serving | attended | the absence justified.
GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Meeting of the Council and a member's attendance`
`an unjustified absence on` d MEANS `Meeting of the Council and a member's attendance` OF d, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE

GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Meeting of the Council and a member's attendance`
`an attended meeting on` d MEANS `Meeting of the Council and a member's attendance` OF d, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE

GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Meeting of the Council and a member's attendance`
`a justified absence on` d MEANS `Meeting of the Council and a member's attendance` OF d, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE

GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Meeting of the Council and a member's attendance`
`an unjustified absence at a subcommittee meeting on` d MEANS `Meeting of the Council and a member's attendance` OF d, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE

-- Three consecutive meetings.
`three unjustified absences in a row` MEANS LIST `an unjustified absence on` (YMD 2026 1 10), `an unjustified absence on` (YMD 2026 2 10), `an unjustified absence on` (YMD 2026 3 10)
`two unjustified absences` MEANS LIST `an unjustified absence on` (YMD 2026 1 10), `an unjustified absence on` (YMD 2026 2 10)
`three unjustified absences broken by an attended meeting` MEANS LIST `an unjustified absence on` (YMD 2026 1 10), `an unjustified absence on` (YMD 2026 2 10), `an attended meeting on` (YMD 2026 3 10), `an unjustified absence on` (YMD 2026 4 10)
`three absences, one of them justified` MEANS LIST `an unjustified absence on` (YMD 2026 1 10), `a justified absence on` (YMD 2026 2 10), `an unjustified absence on` (YMD 2026 3 10)
`an attended meeting, then three unjustified absences in a row` MEANS LIST `an attended meeting on` (YMD 2026 1 10), `an unjustified absence on` (YMD 2026 2 10), `an unjustified absence on` (YMD 2026 3 10), `an unjustified absence on` (YMD 2026 4 10)
`three unjustified absences at subcommittee meetings` MEANS LIST `an unjustified absence at a subcommittee meeting on` (YMD 2026 1 10), `an unjustified absence at a subcommittee meeting on` (YMD 2026 2 10), `an unjustified absence at a subcommittee meeting on` (YMD 2026 3 10)
`three absences in a row of which only two were at the Council` MEANS LIST `an unjustified absence on` (YMD 2026 1 10), `an unjustified absence at a subcommittee meeting on` (YMD 2026 2 10), `an unjustified absence on` (YMD 2026 3 10)

#ASSERT `s 23(c) — the member was absent without justification from three consecutive meetings of the Council` `three unjustified absences in a row`
#ASSERT NOT `s 23(c) — the member was absent without justification from three consecutive meetings of the Council` `two unjustified absences`
#ASSERT NOT `s 23(c) — the member was absent without justification from three consecutive meetings of the Council` `three unjustified absences broken by an attended meeting`
#ASSERT NOT `s 23(c) — the member was absent without justification from three consecutive meetings of the Council` `three absences, one of them justified`
#ASSERT `s 23(c) — the member was absent without justification from three consecutive meetings of the Council` `an attended meeting, then three unjustified absences in a row`
#ASSERT NOT `s 23(c) — the member was absent without justification from three consecutive meetings of the Council` EMPTY
-- FORK F-23c-sub: meetings of a subcommittee are not meetings of the Council (reading A).  The alternative: pass them as Council meetings.
#ASSERT NOT `s 23(c) — the member was absent without justification from three consecutive meetings of the Council` `three unjustified absences at subcommittee meetings`
#ASSERT NOT `s 23(c) — the member was absent without justification from three consecutive meetings of the Council` `three absences in a row of which only two were at the Council`
#ASSERT `s 23(c) — the member was absent without justification from three consecutive meetings of the Council` `three unjustified absences in a row`

-- More than half of the meetings held in the year ending on the removal day 2026-06-30 (window 2025-07-01 to 2026-06-30).
-- 10 meetings, 6 absences: more than half.  10 meetings, 5 absences: exactly half, not more.
`ten meetings in the year, six missed without justification` MEANS LIST `an unjustified absence on` (YMD 2025 8 1), `an unjustified absence on` (YMD 2025 9 1), `an attended meeting on` (YMD 2025 10 1), `an unjustified absence on` (YMD 2025 11 1), `an attended meeting on` (YMD 2025 12 1), `an unjustified absence on` (YMD 2026 1 1), `an attended meeting on` (YMD 2026 2 1), `an unjustified absence on` (YMD 2026 3 1), `an attended meeting on` (YMD 2026 4 1), `an unjustified absence on` (YMD 2026 5 1)
`ten meetings in the year, five missed without justification` MEANS LIST `an unjustified absence on` (YMD 2025 8 1), `an attended meeting on` (YMD 2025 9 1), `an attended meeting on` (YMD 2025 10 1), `an unjustified absence on` (YMD 2025 11 1), `an attended meeting on` (YMD 2025 12 1), `an unjustified absence on` (YMD 2026 1 1), `an attended meeting on` (YMD 2026 2 1), `an unjustified absence on` (YMD 2026 3 1), `an attended meeting on` (YMD 2026 4 1), `an unjustified absence on` (YMD 2026 5 1)
`seven meetings in the year, four missed without justification` MEANS LIST `an unjustified absence on` (YMD 2025 8 1), `an attended meeting on` (YMD 2025 9 1), `an unjustified absence on` (YMD 2025 11 1), `an attended meeting on` (YMD 2025 12 1), `an unjustified absence on` (YMD 2026 1 1), `an attended meeting on` (YMD 2026 2 1), `an unjustified absence on` (YMD 2026 3 1)
`seven meetings in the year, three missed without justification` MEANS LIST `an unjustified absence on` (YMD 2025 8 1), `an attended meeting on` (YMD 2025 9 1), `an attended meeting on` (YMD 2025 11 1), `an attended meeting on` (YMD 2025 12 1), `an unjustified absence on` (YMD 2026 1 1), `an attended meeting on` (YMD 2026 2 1), `an unjustified absence on` (YMD 2026 3 1)
`one meeting in the year, missed without justification` MEANS LIST `an unjustified absence on` (YMD 2026 3 1)
`one meeting in the year, a justified absence` MEANS LIST `a justified absence on` (YMD 2026 3 1)

#ASSERT `s 23(c) — the member was absent without justification from more than half of the meetings of the Council held during the year ending on` (YMD 2026 6 30) `, among` `ten meetings in the year, six missed without justification`
#ASSERT NOT `s 23(c) — the member was absent without justification from more than half of the meetings of the Council held during the year ending on` (YMD 2026 6 30) `, among` `ten meetings in the year, five missed without justification`
#ASSERT `s 23(c) — the member was absent without justification from more than half of the meetings of the Council held during the year ending on` (YMD 2026 6 30) `, among` `seven meetings in the year, four missed without justification`
#ASSERT NOT `s 23(c) — the member was absent without justification from more than half of the meetings of the Council held during the year ending on` (YMD 2026 6 30) `, among` `seven meetings in the year, three missed without justification`
#ASSERT `s 23(c) — the member was absent without justification from more than half of the meetings of the Council held during the year ending on` (YMD 2026 6 30) `, among` `one meeting in the year, missed without justification`
#ASSERT NOT `s 23(c) — the member was absent without justification from more than half of the meetings of the Council held during the year ending on` (YMD 2026 6 30) `, among` `one meeting in the year, a justified absence`
#ASSERT NOT `s 23(c) — the member was absent without justification from more than half of the meetings of the Council held during the year ending on` (YMD 2026 6 30) `, among` EMPTY

-- Two meetings in the year, both missed: all of them, which is more than half (the first-limb list `two unjustified absences` is also a majority).
#ASSERT `s 23(c) — the member was absent without justification from more than half of the meetings of the Council held during the year ending on` (YMD 2026 6 30) `, among` `two unjustified absences`

-- The edges of the window ending on 2026-06-30 (it begins on 2025-07-01): two absences on 2025-06-30 are outside it, two on 2025-07-01 inside.
`two absences the day before the window opens and one meeting attended in it` MEANS LIST `an unjustified absence on` (YMD 2025 6 30), `an unjustified absence on` (YMD 2025 6 30), `an attended meeting on` (YMD 2025 7 15)
`two absences on the first day of the window and one meeting attended in it` MEANS LIST `an unjustified absence on` (YMD 2025 7 1), `an unjustified absence on` (YMD 2025 7 1), `an attended meeting on` (YMD 2025 7 15)
`two absences the day after the removal and one meeting attended in the window` MEANS LIST `an attended meeting on` (YMD 2026 6 15), `an unjustified absence on` (YMD 2026 7 1), `an unjustified absence on` (YMD 2026 7 1)
`two absences on the removal day and one meeting attended in the window` MEANS LIST `an attended meeting on` (YMD 2026 6 15), `an unjustified absence on` (YMD 2026 6 30), `an unjustified absence on` (YMD 2026 6 30)
#ASSERT NOT `s 23(c) — the member was absent without justification from more than half of the meetings of the Council held during the year ending on` (YMD 2026 6 30) `, among` `two absences the day before the window opens and one meeting attended in it`
#ASSERT `s 23(c) — the member was absent without justification from more than half of the meetings of the Council held during the year ending on` (YMD 2026 6 30) `, among` `two absences on the first day of the window and one meeting attended in it`
#ASSERT NOT `s 23(c) — the member was absent without justification from more than half of the meetings of the Council held during the year ending on` (YMD 2026 6 30) `, among` `two absences the day after the removal and one meeting attended in the window`
#ASSERT `s 23(c) — the member was absent without justification from more than half of the meetings of the Council held during the year ending on` (YMD 2026 6 30) `, among` `two absences on the removal day and one meeting attended in the window`

-- Leap edge: the year ending on 2025-02-28 begins on 2024-03-01, so 2024-02-29 is outside it.
`two absences on 2024-02-29 and one meeting attended after` MEANS LIST `an unjustified absence on` (YMD 2024 2 29), `an unjustified absence on` (YMD 2024 2 29), `an attended meeting on` (YMD 2024 6 1)
`two absences on 2024-03-01 and one meeting attended after` MEANS LIST `an unjustified absence on` (YMD 2024 3 1), `an unjustified absence on` (YMD 2024 3 1), `an attended meeting on` (YMD 2024 6 1)
#ASSERT NOT `s 23(c) — the member was absent without justification from more than half of the meetings of the Council held during the year ending on` (YMD 2025 2 28) `, among` `two absences on 2024-02-29 and one meeting attended after`
#ASSERT `s 23(c) — the member was absent without justification from more than half of the meetings of the Council held during the year ending on` (YMD 2025 2 28) `, among` `two absences on 2024-03-01 and one meeting attended after`

-- A meeting before the member was appointed is a meeting of the Council that counts in the denominator, and cannot be an absence.
`three meetings before the appointment and two absences after` MEANS LIST (`Meeting of the Council and a member's attendance` OF (YMD 2025 8 1), FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE), (`Meeting of the Council and a member's attendance` OF (YMD 2025 9 1), FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE), (`Meeting of the Council and a member's attendance` OF (YMD 2025 10 1), FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE), `an unjustified absence on` (YMD 2026 5 1), `an unjustified absence on` (YMD 2026 5 15)
#ASSERT NOT `s 23(c) — the member was absent without justification from more than half of the meetings of the Council held during the year ending on` (YMD 2026 6 30) `, among` `three meetings before the appointment and two absences after`

-- FORK F-23c-year, alternatives.  The discriminating list: two absences early in 2024, then attendance a year and a half later.
`absences in early 2024 and attendance in mid 2025` MEANS LIST `an unjustified absence on` (YMD 2024 1 10), `an unjustified absence on` (YMD 2024 1 20), `an attended meeting on` (YMD 2024 2 1), `an attended meeting on` (YMD 2025 6 1), `an attended meeting on` (YMD 2025 6 10), `an attended meeting on` (YMD 2025 6 20)
#ASSERT NOT `s 23(c) — the member was absent without justification from more than half of the meetings of the Council held during the year ending on` (YMD 2025 6 30) `, among` `absences in early 2024 and attendance in mid 2025`
#ASSERT `s 23(c), alternative reading — the member was absent without justification from more than half of the meetings of the Council held during some one year, among` `absences in early 2024 and attendance in mid 2025`
#ASSERT `s 23(c), alternative reading — the member was absent without justification from more than half of the meetings of the Council held in the calendar year` 2024 `, among` `absences in early 2024 and attendance in mid 2025`
#ASSERT NOT `s 23(c), alternative reading — the member was absent without justification from more than half of the meetings of the Council held in the calendar year` 2025 `, among` `absences in early 2024 and attendance in mid 2025`
-- "Some one year" may start later than the first meeting: the window starting on 2025-11-01 holds seven of the ten meetings, four of them missed (4 of 7 is more than half),
-- although over all ten it is exactly half.  Worked by hand from the text, not read off the module.
#ASSERT `s 23(c), alternative reading — the member was absent without justification from more than half of the meetings of the Council held during some one year, among` `ten meetings in the year, five missed without justification`
#ASSERT `s 23(c), alternative reading — the member was absent without justification from more than half of the meetings of the Council held during some one year, among` `ten meetings in the year, six missed without justification`

-- The combined ground, and the power.
#ASSERT `s 23(c) — a ground for removal by absence exists on` (YMD 2026 6 30) `, according to` `three unjustified absences in a row`
#ASSERT `s 23(c) — a ground for removal by absence exists on` (YMD 2026 6 30) `, according to` `ten meetings in the year, six missed without justification`
#ASSERT NOT `s 23(c) — a ground for removal by absence exists on` (YMD 2026 6 30) `, according to` `ten meetings in the year, five missed without justification`

-- The Minister MAY remove, in consultation with the chair.  Consulted, with a ground: the removal is performance (fields: member | written notice | opportunity | close).
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 23(c) — the Minister may remove the member for absence` "m7" `three unjustified absences in a row` (YMD 2026 6 30) TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Minister` DOES `remove a member of the Council from office` `the Minister` "m7" TRUE TRUE FALSE AT 40

-- EXPECT STANDING remove a member of the Council from office
#TRACE `s 23(c) — the Minister may remove the member for absence` "m7" `three unjustified absences in a row` (YMD 2026 6 30) TRUE AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 400)

-- Without consulting the chair there is no power: nothing stands.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 23(c) — the Minister may remove the member for absence` "m7" `three unjustified absences in a row` (YMD 2026 6 30) FALSE AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 400)

-- Without the ground there is no power either (exactly half missed, no three in a row: no ground).
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 23(c) — the Minister may remove the member for absence` "m7" `ten meetings in the year, five missed without justification` (YMD 2026 6 30) TRUE AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 400)

§§ `Section 23(d): the opportunity to respond`

-- A removal, under (b) or (c), before the member had the opportunity to put arguments in writing breaches (d).
-- EXPECT BREACH s 23(d)
#TRACE `s 23(d) — the Minister must not end a member's term under section 23(b) or (c) before the member had the opportunity to put arguments in writing` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Minister` DOES `remove a member of the Council from office` `the Minister` "m4" TRUE FALSE TRUE AT 20

-- After the opportunity: no breach; the prohibition stands for the next removal.
-- EXPECT STANDING remove a member of the Council from office
#TRACE `s 23(d) — the Minister must not end a member's term under section 23(b) or (c) before the member had the opportunity to put arguments in writing` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Minister` DOES `remove a member of the Council from office` `the Minister` "m4" TRUE TRUE TRUE AT 20

-- EXPECT STANDING remove a member of the Council from office
#TRACE `s 23(d) — the Minister must not end a member's term under section 23(b) or (c) before the member had the opportunity to put arguments in writing` AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 4000)

§§ `Section 23(e): the replacement`

-- The replacement is an appointment under s.20 of a person who may be appointed, as soon as possible.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 23(e) — the Minister must appoint another member to the seat of one who ceased to serve` seat4 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Minister` DOES `appoint a member of the Council` `the Minister` seat4 `a candidate who holds the position and was proposed` EMPTY FALSE TRUE AT 30

-- Appointed, but not as soon as possible: the seat is filled and the duty is breached.
